+// world.js: the closures the overlay's panels read, handed over as bootWorld starts. Each is read when a panel asks
+// (tap.js guards every call: a name declared further down bootWorld answers null until the boot reaches it).
+// Two are DOORS, not reads - the travel panel's, and each is a door the game already has, with its own refusals:
+//   overworld  the TravelView action's own arm (world.js travelViewKey, under the key's `overlayActive` gate)
+//   journey    the Overworld's own click on a place or a spot (world.js onTravelViewPick / beginAcceleratedTravel's
+//              enhanced arm): travelViewAllowed, travelViewCanGo (foes near, a wall, another's boat or wagon), then
+//              travelViewRouteTo / travelViewWalkTo - Travel Options walks it, the clock runs, nothing is skipped. Where
+//              the Overworld owns no journeys (Travel Options off, the classic skin) it is the journal's door instead:
+//              the travel map opened on the place (toggleTravelMap - every refusal the V key meets), Begin left to you.
+// No `//` inside the hook: it is laid on one line.
 const WORLD_ANCHOR = /export async function bootWorld\s*\([^)]*\)\s*\{/;
